      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not so convinced that channel readiness is just for flow control (which I think implies something different) and the spec explicitly states that VW packets are not subject to flow control, so maybe better to reword this. All the traces I\u0027ve seen indicates that this callback (when asserted) indicates that indeed the channel is ready for receiving signals. I think where the problem lies is that we should have been using PLTRST to reset the VW values, and not to  invalidate the signals.",
      "revId": "e1f27a5a35291c2fc06c42f0648c2bc4593d006d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
